n to feel alarmed when I  realized what happens to Zelda in this  whole encounter here we can see what is  presumably the duo's entrance to  Ganondorf holding  chamber note that link is holding a  torch here with zelda holding nothing  the next time we see Zelda she's falling  due to the ground under her feet giving  way but the scene right after shows her  standing calmly next to the Ganondorf  body holding a torch obviously this  isn't shown to us in proper  chronological order otherwise Elda  wouldn't have a torch when she's down by  Ganondorf to me it appears Zelda goes to  ganondorf's body first then retreats  when the body starts twitching to life  the D will make it back to the elevated  ground near the exit but Zelda falls  back down to the level Ganondorf is on  the last thing we see happen is Elda is  how she turns around with a shocked  horrified face on for what she's looking  at while it could be argued that the  scenes shown of Link's gloved right hand  helping Zelda up means that Link pulls  out out of danger unfortunately I don't  think we're that lucky link must have  given Zelda this helping hand before any  of these events took place when they  were climbing elsewhere and here's why  when they enter the chamber link has  both gloves on but when the hand magic  event takes place his glove is removed  if the hand magic link wields in the  trailer happens at any point when the  duo is seeing Ganondorf body as it is  very heavily implied due to the hand  being present on ganondorf's body then  he can't gives out a helping hand out of  where she's fallen because at any point  afterwards he shouldn't have his right  glove on obviously it is possible that I  could be interpreting it wrongly but if  this is true and Zelda is left down here  with a reawakening Ganondorf and no way  back up to safety I think it's probable  that Ganondorf or the malice pouring out  of him or both will possess Princess  Zelda let me explain a couple reasons  why now while thi